# CHUNK 81 Q Z C70 — BLOOM–HALATION INTERACTION ENGINE V6
# ==============================================================================
# Purpose:
#   Bloom and halation are NOT independent in real optical systems.
#   This engine models their interaction:
#
#     • Halation softens Bloom edges (emulsion backscatter)
#     • Bloom suppresses deep halation (light already diffused)
#     • Local highlight density determines which dominates
#     • ACES-compliant multi-layer merge curve
#     • Prevents:
#         - double halo artifacts
#         - spectral oversaturation
