# CHUNK 82 S 03 — MICROCONTRAST TEMPORAL STABILITY
# ==============================================================================
# Purpose:
#   Stabilize microcontrast response over time so fine texture does not
#   shimmer, crawl, or pulse across frames due to noise, motion, or exposure shifts.
#
# Film principle:
#   Film microcontrast arises from emulsion structure and grain clustering,
#   which exhibit strong temporal inertia and do not fluctuate frame-to-frame.
#
# Visible impact:
#   - Eliminates texture flicker
#   - Preserves natural surface detail
#   - Maintains cinematic continuity
#
# Runs AFTER:
